{{Quote|We of the fleet like to think of ourselves as heroes. Often, though, the true heroes are those who design and build the warships we take into battle.|[[Senior Captain]] [[Mitth'raw'nuruodo]]|<ref name="CR">''[[Thrawn Ascendancy: Chaos Rising]]''</ref>}}
[[File:Full-broadside.png|thumb|right|320px|A broadside between two opposing warships.]]
A '''warship''', or '''military starship''', was any [[starship]] designed to engage or participate in [[space warfare]]. Many warships were [[capital ship]]s, [[troop transport]]s, or [[patrol ship]]s.

==Description==
===Overview===
[[File:SWA_The_Corellian_Conflict_box_art.png|thumb|left|280px|Warships of varying size, design, and power participate in naval warfare.]]
A warship, or military starship, was a [[Navy|naval]] [[starship]] designed to participate in [[Space warfare|naval warfare]] as a combatant. Throughout [[Timeline of galactic history|history]], various factions used warships of varying size, type, and purpose.<ref name="Battles">''[[Star Wars: Battles that Changed the Galaxy]]''</ref> Many militaries incorporated warships into service, and outfitted them with weaponry such as [[laser cannon]]s and [[proton torpedo]]es for offensive and defensive purposes, as well as protections such as [[deflector shield]]s.<ref name="Episode III">{{Film|III}}</ref> Beyond armed forces, other groups such as [[megacorporation]]s,<ref name="Episode I">{{Film|I}}</ref> [[pirate]]s, [[Mercenary|mercenaries]],<ref name="Chapter 22">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 22: Guns for Hire}}</ref> and [[planetary defense forces]] utilized warships for their purposes.<ref name="Battles" /> The role of warships varied, as they were designed for combat and could be used for a diverse amount of roles, ranging from conquest and attack,<ref name="Episode III" /> piracy,<ref name="Chapter 22" /> protection, transportation, supply and more.<ref name="Episode III" />

===Roles===
Widely used for combat purposes, warships were used in a multitude of roles. Warships served as [[assault ship]]s, [[battleship]]s, [[command ship]]s,<ref name="Episode III" /> such as the [[flagship]] of a [[fleet]] or [[flag officer]],<ref name="Episode I" /> as [[consular ship]]s in certain instances, as [[dropship]]s, [[evac ship]]s, [[hospital ship]]s [[carrier]]s,<ref name="Battles" /> [[picket ship]]s,<ref name="LE">''[[Thrawn Ascendancy: Lesser Evil]]''</ref> [[supply ship]]s,<ref name="Battles" /> and [[transport]]s.<ref name="MA">''[[Master & Apprentice]]''</ref>

===Classifications===
====Capital ships====
Throughout history, military starship names and classifications were contradictory as shipwrights, guilds, and [[species]] used their own measurements and terminology. Despite this, all classification systems were consistent in classifying a [[capital ship]] as a warship that was 100 [[meter]]s or more in length.<ref name="Battles" />

The [[Anaxes War College System]], which was first implemented during the [[Clone Wars]] that began in [[22 BBY]], was [[the galaxy]]'s standard capital ship classification system. At the [[time]], it introduced three new classes of warship&ndash; the [[destroyer]], the [[battlecruiser]], and the [[dreadnought]]. The classifications instituted by the system were malleable, as warships moved up or down a class based on their armament or role. Beyond this, architects of the system developed a generic shorthand that placed [[corvette]]s, [[transport]]s, and [[starfighter]]s as [[gunship]]s; [[frigate]]s and [[light cruiser]]s as [[cruiser]]s; and larger warships of the line as [[battleship]]s.<ref name="Battles" />

When measuring more granular, capital ships that were between 100-200 meters were classified as corvettes; 200-400 meters as frigates; 400-600 meters as cruisers; 600-1,200 meters as [[heavy cruiser]]s; 1,000-2,000 meters as destroyers; 2,000-5,000 meters as battlecruisers; and 5,000 meters and larger as dreadnoughts.<ref name="Battles" /> Specific models of warships could fall into multiple classes, such as the [[Free Virgillia-class Bunkerbuster|''Free Virgillia''-class Bunkerbuster]] that was considered to be a corvette,<ref name="TLJ VD">''[[Star Wars: The Last Jedi: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref> a frigate,<ref name="TLJ novel">''[[Star Wars: The Last Jedi: Expanded Edition]]''</ref> and a cruiser,<ref name="Episode VIII">{{Film|VIII}}</ref> as well as the [[Subjugator-class heavy cruiser|''Subjugator''-class]] which was designated as a [[heavy cruiser]],<ref name="Malevolence DB">{{Databank|malevolence|''Malevolence''}}</ref> a [[battlecruiser]],<ref name="Battles" /> a battleship,<ref name="Collapse of the Republic">''[[Collapse of the Republic]]''</ref> a [[dreadnought]],<ref name="Ion Cannon">{{Databank|ion-cannon|Ion Cannon}}</ref> and as a [[Star Dreadnought|star dreadnought]].<ref name="Collapse of the Republic" />

====Sub-capital ships====
In addition, [[sub-capital ship]] was used to describe certain warships, though some examples of sub-capital ships<ref name="Lead by Example">''[[Lead by Example]]''</ref> were also considered to be capital ships,<ref name="Battles" /> such as the 282-meter long [[Pelta-class frigate|''Pelta''-class frigate]].<ref name="Rebel Files">''[[Star Wars: The Rebel Files]]''</ref>

====Other warships====
Beyond capital ships, there were other forms of small warships used in naval warfare. These included various types of space-faring [[gunboat]]s such as [[assault gunboat]]s,<ref name="Dawn">''[[Dawn of Rebellion]]''</ref> [[escort gunboat]]s,<ref name="Tarkin">[[Tarkin (novel)|''Tarkin'']]</ref> and [[missile boat]]s. Another type of warship included the [[Corsair]].<ref name="Chaos Rising">''[[Thrawn Ascendancy: Chaos Rising]]''</ref>

====Non-warships used in militaries====
Although not classified as warships, other types of starships could be used for military purposes. [[Freighter]]s were commonly used in combat,<ref name="Episode VI">{{Film|VI}}</ref> as were retrofitted [[yacht]]s.<ref name="Moving Target">''[[Moving Target: A Princess Leia Adventure]]''</ref>

==History==
Military starships, specifically capital ships, were the centerpiece of navies for millennia and whose designs responded to the trends in technological advances and economic incentives.<ref name="Battles" />

In the centuries of peace that preceded the Clone Wars, many large and powerful warships were built by the [[Corellian sector|Corellian]], [[Humbarine sector|Humbarine]], and [[Kuat sector|Kuat]] [[sector]]s to defend their vast industrial riches. Unlike later models, however, their [[hyperdrive]] jump ranges were limited to local.<ref name="Complete Vehicles 2018">[[Star Wars: Complete Vehicles (2018)|''Star Wars: Complete Vehicles'' (2018)]]</ref>

